  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Flood watch this afternoon, higher potential\nsouthern VA into NC. A few strong storms possible.\n\nA front stretches from northern VA into far SW VA. Best low\nlevel convergence exists across northeast TN into southern\nVA/northern NC. Decent low level SRH leading to a few spinning\nstorms, though cloud cover has stabilized the airmass somewhat.\nWill have to watch for strong storms mainly over the NC\nPiedmont/foothills this afternoon. \n\nThe front will be slow moving until a stronger shortwave dives\nsouth into the mid-Atlantic late tonight into Thursday. The\nfront sinks to the NC coast into SC by late Thursday. Still\nample moisture remains and some shortwave energy may keep at\nleast a chance for scattered showers/few storms into the\nweekend.\n\n\nMore on the hydro/flooding in the Hydro section below.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Temperatures at or below normal through the\nweekend.\n\nWith cloud cover sticking around at times and northerly flow\nanticipate highs to be about 10 degrees below normal starting\nThursday into Saturday while lows stay closer to normal.",
